## Alternative source: bulk open data (Données Québec)

The province (MAMH) publishes every municipal assessment roll in Québec as open data:
https://www.donneesquebec.ca/recherche/dataset/roles-d-evaluation-fonciere-du-quebec

- **Format:** one XML file per municipality (~1,140 total). Download all as a ZIP, or one municipality at a time via the CSV index.
- **Latest:** 2026 index + ZIP (March 2026). A quarterly-update index also exists (last updated Aug 2026).
- **Mapping:** georeferenced versions available (2026 in GPKG / FGDB).
- **Update frequency:** annual (plus quarterly updates).
- **Licence:** CC-BY 4.0 (attribution required).
- **Field definitions:** see the "Guide sur les données du rôle" and "Répertoire des renseignements prescrits" PDFs on the dataset page.
- **Contact:** evaluation.fonciere@mamh.gouv.qc.ca

### What's NOT included
- Owner name and postal address (Propriétaire section)
- Cadastre / lot number

These are only available one address at a time on the city website (see above) or at the clerk's office.

⚠️ Re-identifying the redacted owner information is prohibited. 

### Which source for what
- **Bulk data:** screening many properties at once (building characteristics, land area, values)
- **City website:** owner details and lot number for a specific property
